Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||12-07-2000||07:20 AM||||The front scoops are used to relieve the high pressure area that is created behind the radiator.. also, by allowing some of the air to escape through the hood, it reduces the amount of air flowing underneath the car, therefore creating a bit of downforce.<BR>*plus* it looks cool. hehe<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000006||87ECO5||12-07-2000||08:13 AM||||I had the priviledge of seeing Mike's car in person a few weekends ago.  Let me tell you - these photos don't do the car (or Mike's handywork) justice!<P>The car is absolutely beautiful and, IMHO, an image of what the Fiero should have been.  The scoops look right at home and there's no better-looking navy blue paint on a Fiero!<P>Congrats, Mike!  You own a work of art!||||reg||1
