Z||000018||DaRkLoRD||12-09-2000||08:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by VelociFero:<BR><B>I love those Over-the-roof scoops.  Much cleaner than the Toms scoops for the MR2</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There's a guy named Tom that makes MR2 accessories??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>[insert twilight zone music here]  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||6
Z||000019||BOILERMAKER||12-09-2000||08:54 PM||||I won't lie to you.  The mustang vent/scoop took a lot of trial and error contouring it to the hood.  I put a lot of duraglass on.  Those who know duraglass know not to let it set for too long or they have to use 60grit on it.  Well, I let it sit overnight once.  That was a nice learning experience.  But it looks nice now!!!<P>The indy scoop is functional also.  I fabbed up a metal plate to sit between the indy scoop and the decklid.  It has lowered some degrees on my engine as well as the mustang scoop.<P>As far as side scoops, I don't know which ones they are.  They are plastic and have the 3 ribs inside the opening if that helps you out.<P>I thought about the 3 (or really 4th) brake light in they indy scoop, but spent so much time on the mustang scoop that I decided to forget it for right now.  I can always take it off and work on it later.<p>[This message has been edited by BOILERMAKER (edited 12-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||ArmandoP||12-18-2000||09:12 PM||||Boilermaker,<BR>Ill be up in Greenwood this Friday.  wanna get together?<BR>Armando<P>------------------<BR>__________________<BR>will work for MR2 parts!!! <BR>1987 MR2 NA t-bar csp with 700 miles on its new engine. <BR>TRD copper head gasket, milled head .020, 2 short shifters,metal masters rear brake pads, 195-60-14 (soon to get new tires), clear corners, Clevite 77 bearings, NO A/C, MAF relocation mod, red silicon vacuum hoses, redline tranny fluid,and the stock exhaust with a WHOLE bunch of broken welds! <BR>indiana/illinois MR2 owners club<BR>[URLhttp://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/inimoc.html[/URL]<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/mytwo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
